    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.all_node_cuts - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.all_node_cuts.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_node_cuts()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find every minimum node cut of a connected undirected graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.all_node_cuts()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Find every minimum node cut of a connected undirected graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.all_node_cuts()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Find every minimum node cut of a connected undirected graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind every minimum node cut of a connected undirected graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L78486-L78594){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.all_node_cuts()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![All minimum node cuts](../assets/graphs/all-node-cuts.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three copies of a strip of four triangles on A to F, whose node connectivity is 2. Each copy shows one minimum node cut in the accent color, with the edges it removes dashed: B, C cuts off A; C, D separates A, B from E, F; and D, E cuts off F. The card lists the three cuts.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA node cut (or separator) is a set of nodes whose removal disconnects the graph. The\nsmallest ones have as many nodes as the graph's node connectivity\n(`node_connectivity()`), and there can be many of them. `minimum_node_cut()` gives\none cut between two chosen nodes; this method lists all minimum cuts of the whole\ngraph, which shows every way the network's weakest point can be hit: the articulation\npoints when the connectivity is 1, the pairs of nodes that split a ring, and so on.\n\nParallel edges count once and self-loops are ignored. A complete graph has no node cuts,\nso the result is empty.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Every minimum node cut, as a sorted list of node IDs, in sorted order.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is directed or disconnected.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nWith $k$ the node connectivity and $X$ the $k$ nodes of highest degree (Kanevsky,\n1993), every minimum cut is either $X$ itself or separates some $x \\in X$ from a node\n$v$ not adjacent to it. For each such pair, the minimum $x$-$v$ separators form a\nlattice: starting from the one closest to $x$ (read from the residual network of a\nmaximum flow), moving any separator node to $x$'s side and taking the closest separator\nagain reaches all of them, each found once. The work is a few maximum flows per cut, so\nthe method stays fast even when the number of cuts is large. Results match NetworkX's\n`all_node_cuts()`.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~minimum_node_cut`) \n\n:   One cut between two given nodes.\n\n[](`~node_connectivity`) \n\n:   The size of the cuts.\n\n[](`~articulation_points`) \n\n:   The cuts of a graph with connectivity 1.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA ring of six nodes falls apart when any two non-adjacent nodes are removed, so it has\nnine minimum node cuts of size 2:\n\n::: {#ac98df22 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nring = ec.Graph().add_cycle_graph(6)\n\ncuts = ring.all_node_cuts()\nlen(cuts), cuts[:3]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(9, [[1, 3], [1, 4], [1, 5]])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nIn two triangles that share node `C`, the shared node is the only cut:\n\n::: {#e6f724d2 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nbowtie = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [\n        (\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"A\"),\n        (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"D\", \"E\"), (\"E\", \"C\"),\n    ]\n)\n\nlabel = bowtie.get_label_from_id\n[[label(n) for n in cut] for cut in bowtie.all_node_cuts()]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n[['C']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Every pair of closures that splits the core\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network. Its core of 15 stations, the largest\nbiconnected block, survives any single closure, and 15 pairs of closures split it.\nNorthpark, where the lines over the hills meet, is in seven of them:\n\n::: {#c69134bc .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nmetro = ec.metro()\ncore = max(metro.biconnected_components(), key=len)\ncuts = metro.subgraph(core).all_node_cuts()\n\nin_cuts = Counter(n for cut in cuts for n in cut)\nmetro.set_node_attrs(\"in_cuts\", {n: in_cuts[n] for n in core})\nlen(cuts)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n15\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#68ef6a59 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"in_cuts\", color_scale=\"sequential\",\n    label_by=\"label\",\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-8eff6c8a:#406ba2;--ect-a2be67a8:#d1d5db;--ect-66b03f8b:#618fc7;--ect-692e2bbf:#507db4;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-f8094ac6:#79a8e1;--ect-472663e1:#6d9bd3;--ect-6826a5f9:#608ec6;--ect-9d43aea2:#5480b8;--ect-5ee57d66:#4874ab;--ect-3c980f0e:#3c679e;--ect-ec386ef0:#305a91;--ect-97f76ec5:#254e84;--ect-e28c6970:#194278;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-6970a796:#5d7fa7;--ect-7b967146:#2c4a71;--ect-0fa89f73:#929599;--ect-f241547a:#43648b;--ect-5aa54a62:#38577d;--ect-bf50105f:#09254a;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-975840b8:#184f95;--ect-8eff6c8a:#7ea1d0;--ect-a2be67a8:#4b5563;--ect-66b03f8b:#4d79b3;--ect-692e2bbf:#668dc1;--ect-6425850a:#cde2fb;--ect-f8094ac6:#2c5d9f;--ect-472663e1:#3d6caa;--ect-6826a5f9:#4f7ab4;--ect-9d43aea2:#6089be;--ect-5ee57d66:#7297c9;--ect-3c980f0e:#84a6d3;--ect-ec386ef0:#96b5dd;--ect-97f76ec5:#a8c4e7;--ect-e28c6970:#bad3f1;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-6970a796:#103768;--ect-7b967146:#587091;--ect-0fa89f73:#343b45;--ect-f241547a:#35547d;--ect-5aa54a62:#476287;--ect-bf50105f:#8f9eaf;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57